{
  "title": "Residual '+' and parenthesis edge cases in ingredient parsing",
  "description": "Follow-ups left over from the continuation-fragment fix (the \
'+ ...' compound-measurement, footnote, and wrapped-parenthetical handling). \
Remaining known artifacts in data/unique-ingredients.txt and the parsing \
fixtures:\n\
\n\
1. Paren fragments where no safe merge exists: '(16-ounce can chickpeas' \
(source never closes the paren) and '(440-gram) cans' (previous line '2 cups \
white beans, ... 15.5- ounce' is paren-balanced, so the unclosed-paren merge \
heuristic doesn't fire). Also '(about 3 to 3 1/2 ouncesgrated Parmesan cheese' \
(source typo, missing space and close paren). Would need a riskier heuristic, \
e.g. merge a leading-'(' line whose post-paren remainder is lowercase with no \
digits into the previous ingredient.\n\
\n\
2. '1/3 cup + 2 Tbsp (100 mL white vinegar)' parses to an empty item (the \
whole line is measurements), so the empty-item fallback uses the full raw as \
the item. The parenthetical content 'white vinegar' could supply the item \
instead.\n\
\n\
3. '2 T. ice water': extract_unit doesn't recognize 'T.' (traditional \
abbreviation for tablespoon; lowercase 't.' is teaspoon), so '1/4 cup + 2 T. \
ice water' can't fold into a compound amount and the item keeps the '2 T.' \
prefix.\n\
\n\
4. '+ about 6 Tbsp unbleached all-purpose flour': a measurement modifier \
('about', 'heaping', ...) after the '+'/'plus' blocks the compound-amount fold \
because the fold only tries extract_amount/extract_unit. Stripping the \
modifier first (like step 4.5 does for 'or' alternatives) would fix it.\n\
\n\
5. Mid-item '+' continuations like '1 tablespoon olive oil + more for \
drizzling' (item ends up 'olive oil + more for drizzling') and '3/4 tsp salt + \
1/8 tsp' (item 'salt + 1/8 tsp'). Probably wants ' + more' treated like ', \
plus more' (note), and a trailing same-unit '+ fraction unit' folded into the \
amount.\n\
\n\
All are rare (one or two corpus occurrences each); fix only with test coverage \
and a `make pipeline` rerun to confirm the diffs.",
